	ggm@brolga.cc.uq.oz.au (George Michaelson) writes:

>MIT are probing towards X11R6. DEC are cutting the 4.3a CD (if it's not already
>cut) and its not even at X11R5+patches. This is not good.

This is a side effect of the switch to Alpha, which has shifted software
development priorities.  Last year, the Alpha X groups at DEC were actively
tracking the latest sources and the code that is in the field now probably
reflects the X Consortium internal version of X11R5 as of last fall.
Meanwhile the Ultrix group was shrinking, a lot of the remaining manpower
was working on R4000 porting, there were probably plenty of bugs to keep
any number of programmers busy, and the product was soon to enter maintainance
mode (bug fixes only).

I wish DEC would give the SFB driver code to the X Consortium, but last time
I asked there was no chance of that happening.  There might be enough
information out there to reverse engineer the interface (as was done with
Sun GX).  You can get a big performance improvement over a dumb frame buffer
by using just a few hardware operations.

-- 
    John Carr (jfc@athena.mit.edu)


