Yes. And it's in an optional subset. 

>2. Is this going to replace the current "cc" (which I assume doesn't use
>   GEM for backend)?

The current cc doesn't use a GEM backend, correct. One fine day in the
distant future we will go to a GEM based C compiler, but no firm dates
have been set (I personally wouldn't expect it anytime soon).

>3. What is the c89 compiler for? It comes with the C++ distribution.

