Report Distribution Software Needed

We have an accounting system running on an IBM mini (4300 series) that we
are going to abandon in favor of a later version/variant of the same
software on a Vax 4000/300 under VMS 5.52. On the IBM we currently run a
package called 'InfoPac' that creates packages of reports. Each package is a
series of reports that are delivered to an indivual user. Let us say that we
have three reports; reports A, B and C; and that we have four users; Bob,
Sue, Jim and Ernesto. Every day, the following reports must be distributed:
	
	Bob: Report A
	Sue: Reports B and C
	Jim: Reports A and C
	Ernesto: Reports A,B & C

Rather than run multiple copies of reports or sort reports by hand, one copy
of each report is fed to 'InfoPac', which compares each report to an
internal distribution list and assembles packages for each user. We then
print the packages, and get a header sheet for Bob, followed by his reports;
a sheet for Sue, followed by her reports, etc. 

InfoPac has additional features too. Let us say that we print 'Report D'
that has four sections; sections 1 through 4. We can specify that Bob gets a
copy of section 1, Sue gets sections 1 and 3, etc. 

Does anyone know of similiar software for VMS?

At the close of each month, I have 20,000 pages to print and distribute. I'd
like any suggestions of ways to avoid doing it by hand.

Thanks.

							/Andrew

