In article <1993May25.113504.26035@jarvis.csri.toronto.edu>, dw@csri.toronto.edu (Dave Wortman) writes:
> Anyone know a way to make a TK50 disgorge it's tape safely ????

  The "official" method is, believe it or not, to rapidly bobble the load
button (5 or 6 times), ending with it OUT. That should convince the drive
to let go, assuming that you have a logic/servo fault and not a mechanical
jam of some kind.

  Other than that, power cycling should get it to release, at the expense
of possibly damaging the part of the tape in contact with the head at the
time.

  If neither of those do it, then it's either a mechanical problem or a
hard logic failure and surgery will be required.

