  I have no specific information on this device. However, there were a lot
of oddball display devices 8-) developed (or "integrated") by DEC called
"VAXstation" before there were any VAXes in them. Perhaps the most common
is the VAXstation 100, which is a sort of Pro-350-ish-looking box. These
early VAXstations just contained the display adapter, keyboard controller,
etc. and no user-accessible processors (neither VAX nor PDP). Instead, they
relied on a communication link to a VAX system. I believe all of the VAX-
station models less than 1000 (3-digit numbers) were of this style. The
VS100 was a supported peripheral up until VMS V5.0, when the driver support
was removed from VMS.

