	It's quite possible that the error message is correct. I've had lots of
problems with timeouts on our DECnet network. You can use ncp to show you the 
timers and errors that have occured. Tell ncp to "show count node abc" where 
abc is the node you are trying to communicate with. Also tell ncp to "show exec char"
and see what the incoming and outgoing timers are. You can change them with
a "set incoming timer", "set outgoing timer", "define incoming timer" etc.

