In article <1993May17.193755.605@ifwb.w.open.de>, root@ifwb.w.open.de (IfwB) writes:
> We are running a MVax II with a QD33 disk controller connected with two
> Fujitzu disk drives. Our VMS Version is 5.5-1.
> 
> In the past time, we had big problems with our disk drives keeping them
> online. The system is mounting and dismounting the disk drives without
> entering any mount- or dismount command.
> Following message is displayed:
> 
> Broadcastmessage from vax1.w.open.de
> diskstate DUA1: (or DUA2:) offline
> mount verifying in progess   AND SO ON ...  
> 

Any idea how many type of drives Fugi make? Almost certainly hardware. The
QD32/33 tend to get upset and wedge if the drive does anything unexpected.
The common one is drives that seek on a time out to prevent thermal overload
on a few tracks when the drive is idle. The controller then off-lines the
drive when it finds the track has changed, and you need to  off-line/on-line
the drive to reset things properly.

Also check that the A cable is terminated properly, and that the Qbus is
reasonably configured.

~Paul



