Yes - just ten minutes ago I ran a benchmark on a demo Alpha here
in the building. I don't know which configuration it is. The benchmark
consists of rendering a series of images (offscreen), using my own
(optimized source) 3D-routines. Lots of FP in there of course. Result:

Indigo R3000 (!):  12.5 seconds
Alpha:             10.9 seconds
HP735:              5.9 seconds

This was done with cc on Indigo and Alpha, gcc on HP. Gcc on Indigo
is slower than cc, so it's not the compiler that makes the HP faster.

If this mediocre performance is typical for Alpha on real-world
code, then I'm *not* impressed. (FYI, my benchmark consists of
perspective rendering of 65536 vertices/image, 1024x768 8-bit
image, sequence of 84 images from different viewpoints. Data
is mountain landscape.)

The speed of the HP seems okay for that class of machine. It's
not a cheap model :-).

Hope you think this is interesting data - I will mail/post more
if I find more of interest.

