While all manufacturers try to tune their systems as much as possible in
order to make the SPEC ratings come out as good as possible, DEC uses
something called the "Kap Preprocessors" which gives a substantial boost
in performance.  These preprocessors are an extra cost item for Alpha
machines.  

In other words, unless you buy them, you will not get the performance
that the SPECmarks claim.  So if you compare paper to paper but are only
willing to purchase the base machine, then the Alpha ratings are higher
on paper than reality.

Whether this is an issue or not depends on the individual.

