> BTW, is it possible to use the KA630 without RAM boards? I know,
> 1 Mb RAM, no VMS, no Ultrix etc. But it could be possible to use it
> for something else.

Certainly, and lots of them are out there doing realtime apps based on
VAXELN.  VAXELN was originally designed to be able to do useful things,
including the realtime kernel, in 256KB.  At one time Digital had planned
to sell KA630/KA620 boards populated with only that amount as inexpensive
realtime components, but so far as I know they never actually made it to
market.  All the KA630/KA620 boards sold were fully populated with 1MB.

Note: the 50B of BBU RAM mentioned in an earlier note is accessible only
through VAX hardware registers and to firmware, not as general-purpose RAM.

