  It's a bus connecting adjacent slots 8-). On the BA23, it's the first 3
slots; on the BA123, the first 4; on the BA2xx, all of 'em.

  It has power on the usual pins (usual meaning if this was a Q22 slot,
the same pins would be used for power)

> The RLV11 controller used the CD in all-CD backplanes and co-existed
> happilly with other quad Qbus devices (which put at least grant continuity
> into the CD part of the board, in case they're plugged into serpentine or
> zig-zag Qbus backplanes).  Is the KA630 capable of doing this also?  

  Almost all quad cards only use the CD side for power, ground, and bus
continuity (which is done for backward compatibility with non-CD slots).
The continuity lines aren't used for anything in the CD side because 
they might be open, shorted, etc.

