Ahhh, the reasons I dislike (with a passion) TK50 drives!  I had a microVAX
with one that did that a couple of times before I put it out of its misery!!

The method I used to get the tape back.  First, slide the drive out of the 
enclosure and  disconnect the power to the drive.  In the bottom of the drive
you will find an access hole that allows the insertion of a phillips-head screw
driver.  ( I recommend a non-conductive shaft!).  This is the spindle of the 
drive and will let you rewind the tape.  Depending on how much tape is IN the
drive, may I recommend a motorized driver.  Those tapes are long!!! 

Good luck and HAPPY TWISTING !!
