Bill,

I just installed a 1.9GB Seagate Wren on one of our AXP300/400 machines
(running OSF/1). It was fairly straightforward (though as a newcomer to
unix system management, I didn't find the documantation made it *seem*
straightforward!). I just used disklabel to write the default partitions
for an unknown drive, which made the disk usable. The default partitions
were fairly ridiculous (only 3 partitions, the main one being 1.7G in
size) so later when I gained a little more confidence I edited the
partitions to a set of useful sizes, and since then everything has been
running just fine. We also have a smaller (Maxtor, about 600M) drive
attached to the AXP, but it was originally partitioned under Ultrix, so
didn't need any partitions written.

I know this doesn't give much detailed information for you, but I didn't
see any other replies to your question, so at least I can tell you that
third-party drives *do* work! If you have any other questions, send me
mail and I'll try to answer...

