The short answer is "don't".

The "best" way to keep a real live RL02 drive going is to keep a small Qbus
VAX going as part of the cluster; the 3200 would be ideal.

But really, RL02 drives only hold 10MB.  Even if they're all full, a 1GB
SCSI disk is about US$1k, and will hold 100 RL02s worth of data.  Much more
if they're not all full.  The floor space occupied by 100 RL packs will be
worth more than that, to say nothing of the maintenance cost of the equipment.

