Hello all,

	I am looking into picking one of these up (actually, two VS3520's
which I will combine into a VS3540), but I just wanted to know if there was
anyone out there who has one or knows a lot about one. I have the Systems
and Options catalog, so I know what its capabilities are supposed to be,
but there were no X11 performance metrics given for it. I guess production
stopped before DEC started using these metrics...

	Is the VCB03 any faster or slower than the SPX board in a VS3100?
I would sure hope so, being that the price tag was $12k in '90... Also,
I notice that a few VMS products do not support the VS3520/VS3540,
specifically DECdesign and VWS, to name a couple. I know why VWS would
not be supported, but why would a package like DECdesign not be supported?

	A couple questions about the hardware issues of the Q-bus slots. 
There are a few options directly supported (two tape controllers, an asynch
option and a sych option), but no others are listed. Would something like
a 4-plane VCB02 be usable in this system? I would like to run dual-headed,
but if the VCB02 will not work, then that would cause me some amount of
anguish (I am using a dual-headed VS3100 and love it)...

	Is the VS3520/VS3540 going to become unsupported any time before the
turn of the century? I would like to be able to use new releases of VMS
as they become available (that and Motif), but if it goes by the way of
the VAXstation 8000, then it would not be a good thing to have around...

Thanks,
Chris


