>I think "bears no resemblance to anything that came from OSF" is a bit
>strong.  There was quite an effort made to keep the interface,
>management structure, etc. as close to OSF/1 from OSF as possible

	OSF uses setld? lmf? OSF uses Sun's licensed version of NFS
instead of U of Guelph's? OSF uses the MIPSco compiler suite? OSF
unbundles the debugger? OSF has pixie?  Maybe some of these things
have changed recently, so I could be mistaken. I remember back when
OSF was created to respond to USL and put Sun out of business. The
message was "one UNIX. exactly the same from all vendors. totally
compatible."  It was bullshit then and it's bullshit now, only now
it smells stronger. DEC couldn't even keep that promise between 2
of its own platforms, never mind HP, IBM, and the rest. The only
reason the OSF canard has lasted so much longer than ACE did or
COSE will was because it was a new idea then, and the community
hadn't realized what an utter crock the idea of UNIX vendors
cooperating is.

