Well, so much for the fragmentation idea. Is your version of RS/1 compatible
with P/OS v3.n?

There were a LOT of fundamental differences between P/OS v2 and v3, particularly
in the directory structure and logical naming. Also, the use of logical or
physical QIO calls was severely restricted in v3.

Thus, unless your RS/1 docs SPECIFICALLY state that the product is v3
compatible, it probably isn't.

In that case, your only viable alternative is to go back to P/OS v2.


