It is either hardware or a driver/hardware interaction.

To the best of my knowledge (from writing disk drivers back in VMS V2 and V3
days), the cause of mount verification is a driving going off-line. This is
indicated by the driver detecting something in the device registers, usually a
straight-forward operation.

1. The drives are periodically dropping some signal, possibly due to disk
problems or cabling faults. (I'd look especially closely at cabling.)

2. The driver is misinterpreting some signal as indicating an off-line
condition.

I lean strongly toward 1.

