	of TSX+ (that I know of) is V6.40.  There is on-going
	support of RT-11 from digital, I don't know about
	TSX+, it was developed at S&H Computers.

	The system has a limit of 4mb of memory (22-bit address
	space).

>-What can I do with it?

	Being a general purpose computer, you should be able to
	do lots of things.  You may have to write your own
	software for some things, but DECUS has quite a library
	of software for PDP-11's with RT-11 with/without TSX+.

	There are also some software houses which have developed
	languages like C (DECUS also has a C available) or
	networking software like TCP/IP.

	There is also after-market hardware available so that
	you could expand it in several directions.

>-Where can I get additional info?

	Digital may still have manuals available.  Or you could find
	another pdp-11 hacker via these newsgroups who is local to
	you who might let you see his/hers.
	
>-Can I run UNIX on this box?

	Yes, but it will cost ALOT (you'll have to have a source
	license).

>-If so, where can I get a copy? What version?

	USENIX.  You'll have to demonstrate an AT&T source
	license before you can purchase it.  The latest is 2.11BSD,
	which should run just fine on your 11/73.

