 This is my second attempt to collect net.wisdom on DEC's Alpha AXP
machines running OSF/1.  The number of replys I got on the first
net.wisdom posting encouraged me to continue. 

It is posted to comp.unix.osf.osf1 and comp.sys.dec (Followup-To:
comp.unix.osf.osf1) and to the alpha-osf-managers@ornl.gov mailing list.

These lists are my major sources of information.  To suscribe to the
mailing list, send the following command in email to
"Majordomo@SWS10.CTD.ORNL.GOV": subscribe alpha-osf-managers
    
 This posting probably contains some errors is missing many points.
Please send your comments. I'll try to compile a corrected version next
week. 

Some general notes:

There are (at least) two different OSF/1 versions floating around,
called BL10 and BL12.  (See part two, how to distinguish.) BL12 is often
called "production release", too.  They differ in many ways, so don't
forget to specify which version you are referring to. 

Many people have contributed to this list, directly or indirectly.  In
some cases, an answer has been adapted from one or more postings on the
newsgroups or the mailing list.  My thanks to all of you who post and
mail answers and share their experiences with their net.neighbors.  
I added the name of the author of a piece of information if I could
still find out, complain if your name is missing.  The text may have
been edited for this text.

I will try to take care of this list as long as I find the time and when
your responses, corrections, comments, flames and completitions let me
feel you like or really hate it.  I'm looking forward to any response
regarding design and contents of this piece of text or my use of the
english language, which, as you will have noticed, is not my native
language. 

