I'm looking for information about vendors (primarily router and workstation
vendors) that implement the IP Security Options defined in RFC 1108 in their
products.

I already know that Cisco implements the RFC 1108 Basic and Extended IP
Security Options. The manual I have in my office is for release 8.3; has
anything changed with respect to the IP Security options since then?

How about Wellfleet? Other router vendors?

Having the IP Security Options in routers is of only moderate interest if I
can't get the OS in my workstation to generate packets with the IP Security
Options. So, what workstation vendors offer this? Either as a basic part of
the OS, or as an add-on package?

There is an Internet Draft (dated 9 March 1993) for a "Common IP Security
Option". Are there any products available which implement this? Products
close to being available? (Yes, I *know* that this is an Internet Draft,
and thus one cannot claim conformance to it... but I'd still be interested
in any info on products.)

