Ive recently received an LSI-11 in a trade, with an RX02 drive, 
and a load of RT-11 diskettes. When I first tried to power it on,
the console was displaying garbage, so I at first thought that I 
had the console set wrong. I verified the settings of the console
to what is strapped on the card, but I was still getting garbage.

In a fit of frustration, I pulled out all the cards from the backplane,
execpt the processor and the console card, and what-ho, it worked.
I was dumped into the familiar monitor with the @ prompt...

Now I put all the cards in, one at a time. First was the 4 port serial
card (m8043 DLV11?), and that works. Next was the RX02 controller
(RXV11?), and it works. Last is a memory card, but its NOT a DEC
part! Arrgh, and guess what, this is causing the problem.

The card is a dual width memory card, its got green handles, with no
part number stamped on it, and a lable that says 'chrislin industries'.
Theres two banks of 8 DIP switches on the left side. Then there are 
four rows of 8 4116 memory chips (if I remember, these are 16*1, so 
its a total of 64k?).

Outside of that, there is no part number!  If the card is hosed, no
big deal, how much can an MSV11 with 64k cost? but does the above
sound familiar to anyone? probably a bad 4116, but theres no chance
of me having one laying about, and I dont really feel like swapping
32 chips in and out.

Thanx

-- 
