Just a followup to my question a couple of weeks back concerning how to
remove a screaming RD54 from a VaxStation 2000 which is clustered with, and
boots from, a MicroVax II.  I heard back from about a dozen of you and the
results were something close to a consensus:  I need either a genuine RD54
(or other comparable disk, perhaps an RD53?) or some sort of dummy load to
enable the system to boot, and DEC makes (or made) a simple board that
performs the latter function.  I've resolved the problem by moving an RD54
from the MVII boot node to the VS2000.  Everything seems okay now.  I'm
also pursuing the possibility of trading my screaming disk to one of the
respondents for one of the aforementioned dummy boards.  :-)

Many thanks to those who responded:  Bob Marshall, Ken Fairfield, Harvey
Brydon, Roger Ivie, David Cathey, Ehud Gavron (thanks for the additional
tips also!), M. Gaertner, Doug Brune, Carl Lowenstein, Brian Tillman, and
Charles Smith.  Hope I didn't leave anybody out!  (If I did, please let me
know and accept my apologies.  I'll be happy to credit you publicly.)

