                      -< DECraid+ SCSI Storage Subsystem >-
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------


HIGHLIGHTS

o  Improve affordability by using less expensive SCSI drives to lower cost 
   per megabyte of storage

o  New, higher capacity SCSI drives are offered in configuration that 
   certifies support for 140 Gbytes of storage, with potential configuration 
   of 168 Gbytes

o  Complete redundancy of all DECraid+ components optimizes availability by 
   ensuring no single point of hardware failure in subsystem

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new DECraid+ SCSI Storage Subsystem provides a cost effective, fully DSA 
compliant RAID (Redundant Array of Independent Disks) solution that meets 
your storage performance, capacity, sharing, and availability requirements. 
DECraid+ utilizes VAX Disk Striping Driver for VMS software to improve the 
overall performance of I/O throughput by distributing the work across 
several disks. In the DECraid+ storage subsystem, Digital has configured a 
fully redundant 70 Gbyte RAID 0+1 solution. Digital can build any DECraid+ 
SCSI Storage Subsystem from 14 Gbytes up to the maximum of 140 Gbytes.

BENEFITS

o  DECraid+ SCSI uses a rackmountable Hierarchical Storage Controller (HSC65 
   or HSC95), one of the highest performance controllers available for CI 
   based systems. These devices provide fast data throughput.

o  Performance is boosted additionally with disk striping software.

o  DECraid+ SCSI provides very high capacity in a small space.

o  Digital's storage subsystem supports VAXcluster systems, allowing storage 
   to be shared among many users from different CPUs.

o  DECraid+ SCSI uses RAID 0+1 (VAX Volume Shadowing and VAX Disk Striping 
   Driver for VMS software), protecting your data in the event of a disk 
   failure.

o  The DECraid+ SCSI Storage Subsystem is attractively priced.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DECraid+ SCSI Storage Subsystem is available now on a custom quotation 
basis.

SERVICE

Standard list prices include installation or warranty, with either 8 x 5 or 
7 x 24 service. 

TECHNICAL DATA

There are two side-by-side, 81-inch-high H9702 cabinets, each with 1 HSC95 
controller, 12 StorageWorks shelves (BA350-SA), and 20 3.5 Gbyte SCSI disks 
(RZ74-VA). Sixteen SCSI boards are included to allow the HSC95 controller to 
communicate over a SCSI bus with the SCSI drives. DECraid+ SCSI provides 
dual ported access to the 40 drives.

To create a compact, high capacity offering, Digital uses a three phase 
power source, requiring a special five prong plug. The system is driven by 
four power controllers. The power requirement is 208 V for a single cabinet 
and 415 V for two cabinets in the DECraid+ SCSI configuration. 

VMS Volume Shadowing and VAX Disk Striping Driver for VMS software licenses 
are included as subsystem options in the DECraid+ package. The VMS Volume 
Shadowing license is provided for two CPUs of any size.

DECraid+ is supported by OpenVMS V5.5-2, with other versions to follow 
shortly.


