Writer 630 Pro connected to the serial port. Flow control through XON-XOFF is
our only possibility - we do not have the wires to do hardware handshaking.
Flow control seems to work successfully for most jobs sent to the printer.
However, if we send complex Postscript that the printer has to think about for
some time (say 5-10 minutes), lpd seems to time out on being XOFFed, assumes
that some problem has occurred, and resends the job to the printer. The printer
is mesanwhile in the middle of its deliberations, sees that what it is receiving
is irrelevant, and flushes to the end of job, resulting in the print job being
aborted. When I had this problem once before, I connected the printer (actually,
