It's rzdisk -c ask /dev/rrz?a. You will be interactively asked about dozens
of parameters, provided on several pages. One page (I think page 37 or
something) will ask for enable spin-up on poweron. Be aware of not accidently
changing geometry or format parameters. It works only on dismounted disks,
and makes some loud noise. See rzdisk(8).

Hope that helps,
Dietmar
