       We're currently deciding whether we should upgrade to Alphas or
stay with the MIPS platforms.  Toward this end, I put together the
following summary:
 
---------------------------------------------------------------------

                          DecStation 5000              DEC 3000
                         240           260           400      500
	CPU/FPU	        R3000A        R4400         ALPHA    ALPHA 
	SPECmark89	32.4          64.0          108.0    121.0
	SPECint92	27.9          58.0
	SPECfp92	35.8          54.7
	Clock Speed	40MHz         60MHz

        Upgrade Cost from a 240       $4000         $7500    $8800

R4000 Upgrade Cards are priced at $4,000 for the Model 240 board, which uses a
60-MHz MIPS R4400 processor and at $3000 for the smaller board based on the
50-MHz MIPS R4000 processor. 

DEC's current strategy for upgrades from DecStations to ALPHA's is
to charge $99 for your SPECmark89 increase.  So, to go from a DecStation 240
to an ALPHA 400, it costs (108 - 32.4) * 99 = 7500.

The latest Fact Sheet with R4000 data from the 4/20/93 announcement can be 
found on gatekeeper.dec.com: /pub/DEC/DECinfo/DECnews-PR/PR93042004.fs

DEC will not support Ultrix on the Alpha's, but they will continue
to support it on the MIPS machines for the time being.  DEC has NOT decided
whether it will support OSF on the MIPS machines.

The 4000 chips require an upgrade to Ultrix 4.4

