The release notes only say what new hardware is supported.  If something
that was supported becomes unsupported, then it might also mention
that.  In the case of the VAXstation 4000s, it wasn't supported
by previous versions and still isn't.  Probably never will be.

The document that has all the supported systems and other things
is the Software Product Description.  Your kit may have included
a copy.

>
>Is this machine really not supported for ULTRIX - i can't believe it because
>even Vaxstation 2000 are supported.

When the VAXstation 2000 was new, there was little else for ULTRIX
to support.  That was years before the DECstations.  With the
introduction of the DECstation 3100, the whole VAXstation series
became pretty uninteresting compared to generally better performance
of the DECstations.

