In <1s6v03$8as@lll-winken.llnl.gov> oberman@ptavv.llnl.gov writes:

>>	Can I hook up a terminal to a VAXstation 3100 and use it as the
>>console?  I know on the model 38/48/76 there is a switch labelled S3 that
>>enables this.  What about a plain old 3100?  Thanks for your help.

>On all but the oldest 3100s, S3 is present, but unlabeled. It is accessed
>through a small rectangular hole in the rear of the unit. The hole is located
>next to the data comm connector. A few early production 3100s lack this
>feature, but the change was made without any "new model" declaration.

Some models even lack the small hole. You have to (if you really want so) open
the case (2 screws in the backpanel), to lift off the drive plate, to remove
the graphics adapter (if any is present) and finally to remove the CPU-board.
It's a tiny switch located left side facing backwards.

Console mode to serial ports demands a terminal or console printer being
allways on. Turning off the external terminal will cause a halt. Also 
pressing the key labeled <break>. :-) Entering "Continue" mostly allows to
do this. It is interesting to stop the GUI in some cases via this switch
where the <F2>-key isn't working just in time.

