The current 21064 chips are P2.1 or P3.
"P" stands for fabrication pass. Pass 1 chips worked and at speed,
but early software experience suggested a number of subtle improvements
(no instruction set change). 

For more detail, get a copy of the DECchip 21064-AA Microprocessor
Hardware Reference Manual, EC-N0079-72 (1992). Appendix A Design
Enhancements describes the changes in the pass 3 parts. The big topic is
bringing ECC correction logic on-chip; other topics include more flexible
external RAM timing control, support up to 16 MB external cache, read data
acknowledgement, unity stride load miss optimization, clkin/testclkin
circuitry, and about 10 others.
