Unless you are going to put several SCSI drives on the SCSI/2
interface and stripe them, you won't be needing anything faster
than 5 MB/sec.  The faster SCSI drives commercially available
today are only capable of taking data off the media (at the heads)
at an average of about 5MB/sec.  If you are looking for a high
sustained data rate for large sequential tranfers, then I recommend
an IPI subsystem.  It will perform at least twice as fast as SCSI.
If you are doing lots of random I/O, you won't be data rate limited.

Send me email if you want some info on our IPI disk subsystems for
