We are experiencing problems with sending large messages from KINET Decnet product
to DEC VAX.

We try to send API messages from a C-program but find that after ~500 bytes
we get a terrible corruption, which is a repitition of the original ~500bytes
again.

We have checked the ethernet with a protocol analyser and have verified that
this repitition is caused by a duplicate decnet packet being sent across the
link.  Changing the decnet packet size moves the point of corruption!

The problem DOES NOT EXIST with small messages (of 200 bytes).  

Is there a maximum message size to be sent (in one hit) through Kinet?


Below is the test case we are using to write data to remote VAX:

To: :phil
Subject: KiNet write

This is the code fragment I am using.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    length_sent = write ( data_link -> identity_agent ,
        data_link -> text_buffer_out , data_link -> length_data ) ;

    if ( length_sent == -1 )
      {
        timestamp ( stderr ) ;
        fprintf ( stderr , "KiNet send: %d: " , data_link -> identity_agent ) ;
        perror ( "write" ) ; fflush ( stderr ) ;
      }
    else if ( length_sent != data_link -> length_data )
      {
